{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed: Gerrit 3430 merged as 535e09284d37c14fb2944b574b3b618c3fe4df7a. The follow-up for the 5 guard tests that failed on path separators once decoding was fixed is Gerrit 3453, merged as 6140d037413744dcca6633cea91a2b535060decf (test-only: repo-relative paths compared via as_posix()).\n\nWindows sweeps after both landed: job 135569438854 (run 44526811291, main f8e9ea0e61f) and job 135597358757 (run 44534782876, main fa383b1d195). In both, no test from the deleted text-encoding.args failed. The job conclusion is still `failure` because of tests outside this class: 8 MAX_PATH tests in test_plan_review_gate.py (halfcrazed-rubbly-whimbrel), the run_git stdin CRLF test in the earlier run only (scholastic-travelsick-salmon; its test change fed304b2973 is in the later run), and a temp-dir race in test_fixture_env_repr_security (filed as refractive-hasty-iguanodon). Limit of the evidence: the job runs `pytest -q`, so \"passed\" is inferred from the absence of a failure for an un-deselected test, not from a per-test pass line.\n\nNot closing: the AC requires `sweep (windows)` to conclude `success`, and that is blocked by those 3 other tickets."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795101485897494067,"uuid":"1722cae4-7817-4f9b-b477-3ea19ed8510e"}